## [D] THE READING THAT CAUSED ALL OF THIS, and nobody planted it. The devbox, first real
##     run of the version delivered in patch 28.1, verbatim:
##
##       known change at   2026-08-11T05:08:05.098Z
##       reported first at 2026-08-11T05:08:05.096Z
##       lag              -0.00s   (must be >= 0 and <= the 1s interval plus a request)
##       self-test: the instrument reports a change it did not cause, at the second it
##       happened, and its arithmetic answers a question with a known answer.
##
##     Two milliseconds of NEGATIVE lag, reported as a pass. The sighting was timestamped
##     before the request rather than after it, so it could precede the event it reported;
##     and `0 <= d` accepted it only because printf had rounded -0.002 to -0.00. In the
##     sandbox, at a 1 s interval against a fast server, this never once showed.

## [1] break - the sighting taken before the request instead of after, which is [D] made
##     deterministic: the self-test server is slowed past the sampling interval, so the
##     change is guaranteed to land inside a request window rather than 15% of the time.
   2026-08-11T05:12:18.911Z    200   7 Hit_from_cloudfront after                  -           -        - 7b9a72466d39
known change at   2026-08-11T05:12:11.523Z
reported first at 2026-08-11T05:12:10.897Z
lag              -0.63s   (must be > 0 and <= the 1s interval plus a request)
self-test: FAILED - the reported instant does not match the known one (a sighting that is not strictly later than the change is taken on the wrong side of the request).
write->edge      23.0s   (server declares Age 7 and Last-Modified 30 s back: must be 23.0s)
exit=1

## [2] break - the server's Last-Modified moved to 40 s behind Date, so 23.0s is now wrong
known change at   2026-08-11T05:12:28.673Z
reported first at 2026-08-11T05:12:29.810Z
lag              1.14s   (must be > 0 and <= the 1s interval plus a request)
write->edge      33.0s   (server declares Age 7 and Last-Modified 30 s back: must be 23.0s)
self-test: FAILED - write->edge came out 33.0s, not 23.0s.
exit=1

## [3] break - the Age header removed, which is the shape the FIRST version of this
##     self-test shipped in: transitions detected, both computed columns empty, green.
reported first at 2026-08-11T05:12:44.961Z
lag              1.15s   (must be > 0 and <= the 1s interval plus a request)
write->edge      -   (server declares Age 7 and Last-Modified 30 s back: must be 23.0s)
self-test: FAILED - the arithmetic columns were never computed, so nothing checked them.
exit=1

## A FOURTH THING, caught by the self-test itself while the fix was being made and recorded
## because it is the same family: the check extracted write->edge with awk $(NF-2), which
## was correct until the window column was added and then silently read edge->here - 7.4s
## against an expected 23.0s. It went RED rather than quiet, which is the only reason this
## is a footnote instead of a wrong number in the cycle log. The field is taken by index now.
